00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:46.470
A Reunion in Kamogawa

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.310
I wonder what that thing from yesterday was all about?

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.020
You mean about the experiment?

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.110
Yeah. There was that thing with Midori

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.030
and the girl who appeared in my cockpit.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.160
What was she trying to tell me?

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.790
Lan.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.040
What is it?

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.250
Are you afraid of your brother?

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.340
He would never forgive me for seeking asylum.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:19.840
Don't worry. I'm sure Asteria will make things work out.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.550
I hope so.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.350
Are you serious?!

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.850
I wouldn't joke about this.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.060
All right.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.400
Ms. Watabe.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.820
Yes, sir. I will begin preparations right away.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.230
This is going to be fun...

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.780
<i>We've received word that shuttles have departed</i>

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.830
<i>both the Le Garite and De Metrio mother ships with their respective kings aboard.</i>

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.250
I hope this ends without any incident.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.670
Even if a fist fight breaks out,

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:59.340
it's better than having them start a galactic war near Earth.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.060
It's been a while.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.560
You haven't changed.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.690
Glad to see you're in good health too, Captain Tadokoro.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.230
More lady troubles I see, by the looks of you.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.240
Shut up...

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.530
His Majesty, King of Le Garite.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.880
This way, please.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.510
When did you install this?

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.010
Huh?!

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:52.180
Hey.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.650
Did you come alone?

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:00.150
Nah, I'm here with friends. How about you?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.690
I'm here with my subjects.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.070
Regal, as always.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.570
You haven't changed at all, have you?

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.330
It appears the information we have of the two of you

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.950
being best friends since your Academy days is true.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:18.460
We've prepared a quiet location suited for your historical conference.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.380
Please follow me.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.760
Is my younger sister aboard this vessel?

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:29.510
Yes. She and her two friends are engaging in girl talk.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:33.810
What do you say? First one to find them can revoke their asylum status?

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:39.810
Looks like becoming the king has given you a better sense of humor.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.080
So we're starting this already?

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:59.920
What's this for?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.050
Huh? Brother?

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.380
Looks like it worked.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.930
Asteria, why are you here?

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.430
What're you up to?

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.060
You'll see.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.560
Okay, it's showtime.

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:18.390
On my cue!

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.640
Action!

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:28.740
I see...

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.740
So this is the quiet place suited for our historic conference, eh?

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.410
Did you put her up to this?

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:38.460
You think that girl's the type who listens to me?

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:42.210
She wants to hear what the boys have to say.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.250
About our childhood?

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.170
Uh, that's not what I meant...

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.890
But come to think of it, weren't we locked up together like this before?

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:56.770
It was when our shuttle reactor went into overload after failing on a subspace trip.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:00.810
That was the year I went to study abroad at your Academy, so...

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.810
We were both in our first year.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.230
Second year.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.530
We should've just waited for help,

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.690
but thanks to your meddling,

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:11.410
it took them two more weeks to find us.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.280
Except if I hadn't, the ship would've been completely destroyed.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.040
If I was alone, I could have saved it.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.120
So they both went to the same school?

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.670
No wonder they seem to get along.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.550
Doesn't look that way to me...

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.600
Well, well, looks like we're all here.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:39.600
Moid?! And... why're you all here?

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.980
That's what we'd like to know...

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.860
Lord Villagiulio?!

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.820
What are you planning to do here?!

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.480
Silence.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.360
They're in the middle of a conference.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.360
You call that a conference?

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:57.330
I made these special arrangements for those two shy boys.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.620
You should thank me.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.710
Nothing you say will change the Chairman's mind.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.420
Let's just watch and see how it goes.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.050
Did you sleep well last night?

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.260
Why do you ask?

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:17.140
Well, wasn't yesterday the first time you witnessed the power of the Vox?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:21.310
Even when you used your sister for an experiment, I hear you were unable to open the Rin-ne.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:28.400
So I thought the legend might've scared you and kept you awake.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.940
Just like when you were a kid.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:32.940
My brother was also scared?

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:34.860
Aren't you glad?

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.870
He's a scaredy-cat, just like you, Lan.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.330
Yes.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.370
You're right, I didn't get any sleep.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:44.250
I was too excited.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.210
Oh?

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:51.210
With that power, I can solve the 1,000-year problem.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.970
Damn you!

00:08:58.390 --> 00:08:59.850
Quiet!

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:08.060
Seems the rumors about you wanting to use the Vox to destroy our planet are true.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:12.530
I only wish to avert the disaster.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.450
You lost family.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.280
You, more than anyone, should know the danger of the Vox.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.450
But rest assured.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:25.660
Under our research and care,

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.880
we can expand on Vox Aura's potential.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.920
We can avoid further tragedy.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.510
After all, Aura's pilot is special.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:38.680
I'm... <i>special?</i>

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.600
Looks like he's finally revealing his true feelings.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.850
<i>I see...</i>

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:48.600
If you're really that into Madoka, then I may need to change plans.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.610
Hell, why don't we just fight over her as warring nations?

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:53.020
Well?

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:55.280
That's fine by me.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.200
An unregistered aircraft has left the Le Garite mother ship

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.410
and is headed this way.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:04.620
Jim?{he's dead}

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.500
No response from the Occupation Forces, ma'am.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.250
They're letting it through. Get me through to Cap.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.630
Tadokoro here.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.460
From Le Garite?

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.800
Hey, look!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.550
An Ovid?!

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.520
Care to explain, Moid?

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.650
That's some pretty bad flying.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.610
It's one of your pilots.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.320
No complaints if we take care of it, right?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.990
Be my guest. Go easy, though.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:41.870
Wow...

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.990
It's flying all over the place.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.910
That pilot sucks.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.040
Not that I'm any better, but still.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:48.620
Oh no!

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:51.630
That direction! It's headed for Kamogawa!

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.960
What?!

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.590
Can I get a Kamopaccio, please?

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:57.920
Sure. One Kamopaccio coming right up!

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.680
Hey Izo! It's burning.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.430
Oh no!

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:04.050
Hot!

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.390
You worried about that thing from yesterday?

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:08.850
Hell yeah.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:12.310
If what happened on Militia happens on this planet,

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:14.730
think how many people would die!

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:19.690
The king of Le Garite and Villagiulio are in talks to avoid just that.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.990
Yurikano paved the way for this.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.950
Let's have faith.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.750
How many more of these Sangayaki Lunch Specials do we need?

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.460
Three more.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.840
An Ovid!

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.380
A Le Garite production model!

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.590
Oh crap, I think it's coming right at us!

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.260
Everybody, run!

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.770
It's down!

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:00.780
Lan.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.030
Big Brother!

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.030
Brother!

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:05.950
You look busy.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.580
Uh, yeah. Gotta get to Kamogawa...

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.870
Sorry. I'll talk to you later!

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.250
Forgive me.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:21.880
What the hell is Le Garite thinking?!

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.590
Do you suppose they're here for the conference?

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.640
Whatever the case, they're nuts!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.720
Hey, you! Le Garite pilot! You can hear me, right?!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.310
Are you out of your mind?!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.770
This is Kamogawa...

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.860
a designated neutral zone of De Metrio and Le Garite!

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:41.570
Ow... I hurt my butt!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.280
Yurikano, is that you?

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.450
Yep, it's me!

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.000
Dammit!

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.090
Take your hands off of me!

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.840
I have to speak with her!

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:04.920
Let me go, dammit!

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:06.220
Yurikano!

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.840
It's me! Array!

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.760
Why don't you recognize me?!

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.060
Yurikano...

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.530
Yurikano!

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.660
I'm so sorry, Lord Dizelmine.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.540
I broke your promise and came here anyway!

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:36.580
You are such a bad girl, Yuriyuri.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.000
Yuriyuri?!

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:43.090
The princess of De Metrio?!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.880
Her?!

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:45.920
Yes...

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.640
She's Villagiulio's real younger sister.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:53.810
Oh, but I know that in his heart, he considers you as his little sister, Muginami.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.940
So don't worry about which of you two he loves more.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:00.900
Look, Lan. That's not the problem right now.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.900
I see. His real sister, huh?

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.070
We get it, Madoka!

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:10.780
But Lan, what was Yurikano doing on Le Garite?

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:11.740
I don't know.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.870
Didn't you come on the same ship?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.910
No...

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:16.830
Lan?

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:21.670
I met Lady Yurikano several times when I was little.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:24.090
But I never saw her on the ship.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.220
I didn't even know that we were on board together.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:32.260
My brother didn't say anything during our trip here.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.430
So it was a secret.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:37.020
Explain yourself!

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.940
It means your younger sister is alive.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.480
I'm asking why she was with the Le Garite!

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.400
I rescued her from the Tragedy of Militia Zodia.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:50.860
While you were busy leading some rogues and calling yourselves Kiss.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:51.870
Don't mess with me!

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.580
For a while, I feared she wouldn't make it,

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.370
but {we finally managed to heal her up to this point.}she finally managed to recover as you can see.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.880
As her older brother, shouldn't you be happy for her?

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.130
Older brother?

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:10.260
That's right. This man is your real older brother, Yuriyuri.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:14.390
Um... I...

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.220
She doesn't remember a thing?

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:21.100
No. Not even about her being the princess of De Metrio.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.610
Lord Villagiulio.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:26.020
Biotelemetry numbers are normal.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:29.240
Her DNA pattern is a perfect match with Lady Yurikano.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:32.030
She's not a clone.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.740
But she's changed so much.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.160
It's hard to believe it's her!

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.240
It's her all right.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.790
No doubt about it. I can tell.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:44.630
She's behaving exactly like when she was a little kid.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.000
Right down to calling herself Yuriyuri.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:50.920
We're going home!

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:51.340
Huh?

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:54.140
Aren't you going to try to stop them?

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:55.800
No!

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.100
I'm not leaving without Lord Dizelmine!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:05.230
I see you've trained her well.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.190
Don't be ridiculous.

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:09.030
More importantly, what about our conference?

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:10.780
Although it was our fault,

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:13.450
I think continuing the talks might be difficult.

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:16.200
I suppose you're right.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.450
We shall meet at the Intergalactic Conference.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.210
If you'll excuse us, then.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:29.380
Lord Villagiulio!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.510
Are you just going to let them go like this?!

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:32.920
Shut up!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.260
Please don't talk to me right now.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.510
She's terrible!

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:41.350
Calm down, Muginami!

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:45.480
But! But I feel so sorry for Brother!

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:47.060
I'm sorry.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.690
You have nothing to apologize for, Lan!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.110
I know, but...

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.900
Okay! Let's go and see them.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.240
Huh? Right now?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.240
We should act now while it's still fresh in our minds!

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:57.820
Huh? But...

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:58.990
Let's go!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.660
May I ask you one question?

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:06.420
Was all this commotion part of your plan?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.670
Well...

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:08.920
Just a minute!

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.670
I'd like to speak with Miss Yurikano.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:17.930
Yesterday, you appeared in my cockpit, didn't you?

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:18.970
Cockpit?

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:23.520
Mind telling me what this is about, Miss Kyouno Madoka?

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:25.480
Yesterday, during the course of our experiment,

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:28.150
she appeared in the cockpit of Aura.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:32.570
That's very odd. She was with me the entire time.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:34.690
But that was definitely Miss Yurikano.

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:36.610
Well, Yuriyuri?

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:40.070
Do you recall meeting with Miss Madoka?

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.500
You... are...

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.540
Uh-huh. Do you remember me?

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:49.500
No, I don't know you. {lol this was a nice troll}

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.290
What?!

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:55.760
Even after you grappled and tussled me like that?!

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:58.970
Oh yeah! What about before that?!

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:00.300
We also met another time!

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:02.260
Stop right there.

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:03.680
Hold on, Asteria.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.980
I've heard enough. Now's not the time.

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.900
Let's go.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.320
For now, I guess we'll do as she says.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:35.960
Let's go.

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:36.800
Right.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.760
How'd it go?

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:44.220
She's definitely that girl. I'm positive!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:47.230
But if she's the real Miss Yurikano,

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:50.190
shouldn't she act more unwilling?

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:52.560
That's why we need to have a proper talk with her!{realtalk}

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.900
Otherwise, Big Brother Giuvi and Lan's brother will...

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.440
Then let's sneak in!

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:58.360
Huh?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.030
Sneak in where?

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.740
If we stay here, you'll never get a chance to talk.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.990
Don't worry. Just leave it to me.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.920
Lady Yurikano is on board.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:19.050
We will continue negotiations regarding Lady Lan.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:20.050
Moid.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:20.930
Yes?

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:22.760
I thought I told you to assign

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.720
more chaperons to Yurikano, did I not?

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.350
I'm terribly sorry!

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:30.180
Although, it <i>did </i>allow us to gather some unexpected information.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:31.810
Yes.

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:32.810
Brother!

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.690
Please wait!

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.520
Lan?

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:40.700
Brother...

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.110
I would like to return to Le Garite...

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.160
with, uh... my friends.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.910
'Scuse us, coming through.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.620
Oh my.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:57.380
Never been to Tokyo, but outer space just fascinates me.

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:01.920
I've been begging Laffy to take me there with her...

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:04.640
Oh, you can call me Success.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.970
And this here is...

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.640
Suzuki Namie.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.980
Do you mind?

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:12.560
Of course not.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.480
Thanks a bunch, really!

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:14.480
Thank you!

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.610
Is it all right to let them go?

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:21.570
Of course not...

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.950
Come on! We're in a big hurry!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.530
I know!

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:32.290
But that's no excuse for me to manhandle my fishnet!

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:35.540
To a fisherman, they're nearly as dear as life itself.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:40.710
You guys should know that by now after being in Kamogawa for so long!

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:41.800
Oh yeah...

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.430
So Izo, when are you going to ask Sachi out to the movies?

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:46.340
I never made such a promise!

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.640
Come on! How tangled can these nets get?!

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:53.600
Oh no! The Le Garite shuttle's taking off!

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.900
Damn! This can't be happening!

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.820
Yurikano!

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.360
Whoa! How freakin' awesome!

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:08.030
So <i>this</i> is outer space!

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:10.280
Success says, "Wow"!

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:11.910
"Just leave it to me", she said.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:13.540
Super amazing. yeah?

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.460
"After all, I'm a member of Kiss", she said.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:15.460
This is crazy, yeah?!

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:17.500
I think she's having a lot of fun.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:19.210
Super amazing, yeah?

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.210
Fun?! I feel sorry for her!

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.840
You can take off those disguises now.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.420
Miss Madoka. Miss Muginami.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:30.470
Right...

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.980
What do we do now?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:44.320
It seems Dizelmine is hellbent on going to war with me.

